.TH "libnvme_sed_discover" 9 "libnvme_sed_discover" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvme_sed_discover \- Retrieve the TCG Level 0 Discovery data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "int" libnvme_sed_discover
.BI "(struct libnvme_transport_handle *hdl "  ","
.BI "void *buf "  ","
.BI "__u32 len "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "hdl" 12
Transport handle
.IP "buf" 12
Buffer for the Level 0 Discovery data
.IP "len" 12
Size of \fIbuf\fP in bytes
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Issues a Security Receive for the Level 0 Discovery ComID. The data
is returned unparsed; use \fBlibnvme_sed_l0_for_each\fP or
\fBlibnvme_sed_l0_find\fP to walk the feature descriptors.
.SH "RETURN"
0 on success, the NVMe command status if a response was
received (see \fIenum nvme_status_field\fP) or a negative error code
otherwise.
